What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/.../uma/donated_memory_bytes
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Contact:	AMD GPU maintainers <amd-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org>
Description:
		The amount of the device's firmware-reserved UMA carveout, in
		bytes, that is currently owned by Linux as System RAM.

		Writing a larger or smaller value transfers memory from the GPU
		to Linux or from Linux back to the GPU.  Values must be multiples
		of donation_block_size_bytes and must not exceed
		donatable_memory_bytes.  A multi-block request commits one block
		at a time.  If a later block cannot be transferred, the write
		returns an error and a subsequent read reports the amount actually
		transferred.  Donated blocks are onlined into ZONE_MOVABLE.

		Direct state changes through the donated blocks' memoryX/state
		attributes are rejected.  Ownership must be changed through this
		attribute so the GPU exclusion guard, CPU mappings, and memory
		hotplug state remain synchronized.

		The attribute is present only when the amdgpu device supports the
		experimental reversible UMA donation mechanism.

What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/.../uma/quarantined_memory_bytes
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Contact:	AMD GPU maintainers <amd-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org>
Description:
		The amount, in bytes, protected by an exact GPU allocation guard
		but not currently exposed as System RAM.  A nonzero value records
		an incomplete cache-attribute or ownership transition.  Repeating
		a write to donated_memory_bytes first repairs the boundary block
		toward the requested owner.

What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/.../uma/donation_block_size_bytes
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Contact:	AMD GPU maintainers <amd-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org>
Description:
		The memory-hotplug block size, in bytes, used as the transfer
		granularity for donated_memory_bytes.  The value is determined at
		runtime and is not assumed to be identical across systems.

What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/.../uma/donatable_memory_bytes
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Contact:	AMD GPU maintainers <amd-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org>
Description:
		The maximum amount, in bytes, of the device's firmware-reserved UMA
		carveout which can be donated.  The driver selects a
		memory-block-aligned physical interval that does not overlap pinned,
		kernel, or VRAM-manager-reserved allocations during initialization.

What:		/sys/bus/pci/devices/.../uma/donation_range_start
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Contact:	AMD GPU maintainers <amd-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org>
Description:
		The CPU physical start address of the donatable interval, reported
		in hexadecimal.  Donation grows down from the interval's high end,
		keeping the Linux-owned portion contiguous.
